e 2,9 a 6,2. En diciembre se adjudicó el 11 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 10 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 34 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.671,47 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede deberse a mercados estables o necesidades específicas. No refleja actos ilícitos ni decisiones equivocadas.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos al límite abarcan la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas similares. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se ajustan a presupuestos cerrados o a demandas específicas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 54 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 12.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.9 to 6.2. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 10% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 7. Contract [1], for 14,671.47 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar distribution could result from routine scheduling. Small amounts near the limit may reflect market rates or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts cover the same need. Review awardee A’s contracts for patterns. Verify if December’s high volume reflects normal annual trends.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["BS5eC8r8X7i9Hd5zqvq9cg%3D%3D","H5Juk2Oiv